# A map literal writes an atom key bare — `{ a: 1 }` — so `inspect` must not
# double the atom's colon onto the key separator and produce `{ :a: 1 }`,
# which is not syntax the parser accepts (issue #212).

main do
  IO.printLine({ a: 1 }.inspected)
  IO.printLine({ a: 1 }.showValue)

  # A string key keeps its quotes under inspect, which round-trips too; show
  # drops them, as it drops quotes everywhere.
  IO.printLine({ "a": 1 }.inspected)
  IO.printLine({ "a": 1 }.showValue)

  # Atoms outside the key position are unaffected.
  IO.printLine(:a.inspected)
  IO.printLine([:a, :b].inspected)
  IO.printLine({ a: :b }.inspected)
end
